export anchor ProjectsDashboard:
    description:
        The home screen after sign-in. Every style in the library draws this
        screen with the same content, so the styles can be compared fairly.

    navigation:
        - Home, the current page
        - Projects
        - Tasks
        - Team
        - Reports
        - Settings

    header:
        A search field for projects and tasks, a New project button, a
        notifications control and the signed-in user, Mara Okafor.

    greeting:
        A greeting with the user's first name and the date, Saturday 31 October
        2026, plus one line that names the most urgent fact: 4 tasks are
        overdue.

    summary:
        activeProjects: 6
        tasksDueThisWeek: 23
        overdueTasks: 4
        hoursLoggedThisWeek: 186

    projects:
        - Website redesign, Design, 72 percent, 18 of 25 tasks, due 14 Nov, on track
        - Mobile app 2.0, Engineering, 45 percent, 27 of 60 tasks, due 2 Dec, at risk
        - Q4 customer survey, Research, 90 percent, 9 of 10 tasks, due 7 Nov, on track
        - Billing migration, Engineering, 30 percent, 12 of 40 tasks, due 20 Nov, behind
        - Spring catalogue, Marketing, 15 percent, 3 of 20 tasks, due 15 Jan, on track
        - Onboarding emails, Marketing, 60 percent, 9 of 15 tasks, due 21 Nov, on track

    statuses:
        Each project has one of three statuses, On track, At risk or Behind.
        A status always shows its word, and its icon or symbol differs in shape,
        so the meaning never depends on colour.

    activity:
        - Jonas Weber completed "Export invoices as CSV" in Billing migration, 12 min ago
        - Priya Nair commented on "Hero image options" in Website redesign, 40 min ago
        - Sam Ortiz moved "Push notifications" to Review in Mobile app 2.0, 1 h ago
        - Lena Fischer added 3 tasks to Spring catalogue, 2 h ago
        - Tomás Ruiz logged 6 h on Mobile app 2.0, 3 h ago
        - Aiko Tanaka uploaded survey-results-v2.pdf to Q4 customer survey, yesterday

    chart:
        Tasks completed per day over the last 14 days, from Sunday 18 October
        to Saturday 31 October. The values are 3, 12, 9, 14, 11, 8, 2, then 4,
        15, 13, 17, 12, 10, 2. Last week totals 59 and this week totals 73.
